{#- #980. One line, no dashboard. Origami's members learned of every outage
    from a Slack message after the fact; a Prospektor member whose screen said
    *reconnecting* had nowhere to look. This page reads the studio's own
    heartbeat record (GET studio.prospektor.ai/api/status, written every five
    minutes) and says up, degraded since when, back since when, or that nobody
    has checked lately. status.js writes the two lines; the words a visitor
    sees before it answers are the ones below. Out of the sitemap and noindex
    on purpose: it is a utility, not a page to rank. -#}
<section class="onboard">
  <div class="onboard-inner">
    <div class="onboard-panel" id="status" data-api="https://studio.prospektor.ai/api/status">
      <div class="scan-result-meta" id="statusMeta">status · studio.prospektor.ai</div>
      <h1 class="onboard-h1" id="statusLine">Checking.</h1>
      <p class="onboard-sub" id="statusNote">Asking the studio now.</p>
      <p class="onboard-sub">Signed in and stuck while this says up? <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a> reaches a human.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

